  $SCRIPT_NAME help                              Show this message

Hooks:
  <repo-root>/.wtree/config.json defines commands to run around 'add'. Actions
  are timed, and a failing one is reported at the end while the rest still run.
  'init' writes the file with both hooks empty. Needs jq.

    pre-add    runs from the repo root, before anything is created.
               If an action fails, the worktree is not created.
    post-add   runs from the root of the new worktree.
               Failures are reported, never rolled back.

  Each action gets \$WTREE_EVENT, \$WTREE_NAME, \$WTREE_BRANCH, \$WTREE_PATH and
  \$WTREE_ROOT, and starts in its own subshell, so a 'cd' never leaks onwards.

  {
    "hooks": {
      "pre-add":  { "actions": [] },
      "post-add": { "actions": [
        { "type": "bash", "command": "pnpm install" }
      ] }
    }
  }
